WEBVTT

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:03.770
You're allowed access to the majority of the facilities.

00:00:02.230 --> 00:00:06.820
Chapter 6:

00:00:02.230 --> 00:00:06.820
War Correspondent, Hard Struggle!

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:07.500
But, the armory and intelligence-related facilities are off-limits.

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:09.550
In order to ensure confidentiality, we will be

00:00:09.550 --> 00:00:12.460
checking all of your photographs and documents here.

00:00:12.790 --> 00:00:14.280
If you have any concerns,

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:15.930
the public relations department will help you.

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:17.720
Do you have any questions?

00:00:18.730 --> 00:00:20.430
No, none at all.

00:00:20.430 --> 00:00:22.220
Then, please sign here.

00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:24.560
Yes, I'll be glad to.

00:00:25.990 --> 00:00:27.490
Thank you!

00:00:32.690 --> 00:00:35.650
<i>I've finally come to the Amatriain Base.</i>

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:38.530
<i>There's a great scoop here.</i>

00:00:38.530 --> 00:00:40.400
<i>The man who's in the spotlight among the Militia...</i>

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:44.200
<i>no, among the whole of the Gallian Army...</i>

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:48.580
<i>Lieutenant Welkin Gunther.</i>

00:00:49.270 --> 00:00:52.260
<i>I'm going to strip you bare!</i>

00:00:54.230 --> 00:00:57.820
I'm Irene Ellet, a war correspondent from Radio GBS!

00:00:58.240 --> 00:00:59.800
Oh...

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:02.260
Wow.

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:06.370
She's a beauty. Who's she?

00:01:06.370 --> 00:01:07.980
Oh, you don't know?

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:09.210
You know her, Jann?

00:01:09.650 --> 00:01:12.820
She's a war correspondent who's a real rising star.

00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:15.880
It's said that she's willing to risk her life for a scoop.

00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:18.690
She'll risk her life... eh?

00:01:19.190 --> 00:01:21.690
I hear she's an outstanding reporter.

00:01:21.690 --> 00:01:24.890
I wonder what she came here to find.

00:01:24.890 --> 00:01:27.040
An interview?

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:34.280
Yes. I want to conduct interviews for Squad 7,
especially with Lieutenant Welkin Gunther as my focus.

00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:42.090
<i>It's true that, in the eyes of strangers, Welkin has many military achievements, and he does look like an outstanding officer...</i>

00:01:42.090 --> 00:01:43.800
<i>But the truth is...</i>

00:01:44.350 --> 00:01:47.560
<i>He's absentminded, difficult to understand,</i>

00:01:47.560 --> 00:01:49.980
<i>and has a weird animal fetish.</i>

00:01:49.980 --> 00:01:53.470
<i>If the public finds out about that, the Militia's reputation will plummet!</i>

00:01:53.470 --> 00:01:58.560
<i>Although only Welkin should be held responsible, the blame will be pushed onto all of Squad 7.</i>

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:02.500
<i>Besides, as Welkin's assistant officer, I'm also partly responsible...</i>

00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:06.420
<i>I have to reject this interview!</i>

00:02:06.420 --> 00:02:10.120
So, thanks for your assistance!

00:02:10.120 --> 00:02:11.250
Sure, you're welcome.

00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:13.940
<i>Why the heck did he say 'okay' without talking to me first?!</i>

00:02:13.940 --> 00:02:15.340
I really appreciate it.

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:21.070
So, I'll be sticking close to Squad 7 for the time being!

00:02:21.070 --> 00:02:25.360
<i>I couldn't protect Squad 7's reputation...</i>

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:27.900
<i>No, I mean the Militia's reputation!</i>

00:02:27.900 --> 00:02:31.730
<i>I mustn't let them be together by themselves!</i>

00:02:31.730 --> 00:02:36.980
<i>I have to watch over Welkin so that he doesn't say anything strange!</i>

00:02:38.230 --> 00:02:43.110
Well then, for starters, do you mind if I
ask why you volunteered for the Militia?

00:02:43.110 --> 00:02:45.140
Sure. About that...

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:47.530
It's the basis of universal conscription!

00:02:47.530 --> 00:02:50.180
It's in accordance with benevolence and love for our homeland!

00:02:50.180 --> 00:02:56.080
As such, in order to stop the Imperials' invasion and return Gallia to peace once more! {this and last sentence doesn't connect. edit pls}

00:02:57.540 --> 00:03:01.220
Umm... I was asking your squad leader.

00:03:01.220 --> 00:03:03.570
That's what our squad leader said before!

00:03:03.570 --> 00:03:04.780
Huh?

00:03:04.780 --> 00:03:06.380
Right?

00:03:06.380 --> 00:03:07.760
Oh, did I?

00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:09.460
Right?

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:11.680
So she says.

00:03:13.330 --> 00:03:17.390
Next, I'd like to ask you about the battle at Vasel Town.

00:03:17.390 --> 00:03:21.210
That battle was probably your first experience of combat.

00:03:21.210 --> 00:03:23.090
So what do you honestly think was the key to that victory?

00:03:23.540 --> 00:03:27.280
That was originally meant as a comeback for an insult...

00:03:28.030 --> 00:03:35.370
That's not true! Squad 7 was well-coordinated and
took action according to his swift and calm judgment.

00:03:35.370 --> 00:03:39.840
That's the most important cause of victory, said my squad leader!

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:42.710
So she says.

00:03:42.710 --> 00:03:45.280
Say, can you leave us alone?

00:03:45.660 --> 00:03:51.240
Unfortunately, I'm the assistant officer of Lieutenant Welkin Gunther of Squad 7!

00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:55.170
It is my duty be with the squad leader at all times!

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:56.510
Really?

00:03:56.510 --> 00:03:57.830
Yes, really!

00:03:57.830 --> 00:03:59.330
So she says.

00:04:04.990 --> 00:04:08.340
<i>Geez, it's really hard to do my job.</i>

00:04:08.340 --> 00:04:11.930
<i>With her tagging around, I can't even do a proper interview.</i>

00:04:11.930 --> 00:04:19.150
<i>But... If his lapdog is that jittery, it's like she's telling me there's something that mustn't be made public.</i>

00:04:19.150 --> 00:04:23.400
Just you wait! I'll definitely get my scoop!

00:04:23.820 --> 00:04:27.380
But before that, let's go deal with the pawns first!

00:04:32.490 --> 00:04:33.890
I'm exhausted...

00:04:33.890 --> 00:04:37.560
What's wrong, Alicia? You look tired.

00:04:37.560 --> 00:04:40.660
Just whose fault do you think that is?

00:04:40.660 --> 00:04:41.710
Whose?

00:04:41.710 --> 00:04:43.530
It's all your fault!

00:04:44.570 --> 00:04:45.990
Really?

00:04:47.170 --> 00:04:48.720
O-Of course.

00:04:49.120 --> 00:04:53.400
Look, you mustn't say anything weird in front of Miss Ellet!

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:55.980
The Militia's reputation is at stake here!

00:04:55.980 --> 00:04:57.560
Reputation, huh?

00:05:00.020 --> 00:05:05.400
But if that's the case, shouldn't we inform the rest of Squad 7 in advance?

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:10.080
If it's an interview, everyone will surely tell her many things.

00:05:15.680 --> 00:05:17.020
I have do something!

00:05:18.170 --> 00:05:19.770
Sergeant Melchiott.

00:05:21.810 --> 00:05:23.160
We're on standby.

00:05:23.160 --> 00:05:24.190
Don't run in the corridor.

00:05:24.650 --> 00:05:26.200
I apologise, Madam!

00:05:26.200 --> 00:05:31.370
You came just in time. I want to talk to you about Squad 7's interviews.

00:05:31.370 --> 00:05:34.620
<i>What's bothering me are those interviews!</i>

00:05:35.260 --> 00:05:38.810
First, please tell me about Lieutenant Gunther.

00:05:38.810 --> 00:05:42.450
Well, let's see... He's an incredible guy.

00:05:42.450 --> 00:05:46.050
More importantly, can you let me say something about vegetables?

00:05:46.920 --> 00:05:50.360
I'm actually quite picky about vegetables even though I don't look like it.

00:05:50.360 --> 00:05:51.640
The wonder of vegetables-

00:05:51.640 --> 00:05:55.100
Who the hell wants to hear about vegetables?!

00:05:55.100 --> 00:05:58.010
Anyway, let me sing a song!

00:05:58.010 --> 00:06:01.060
I was a singer at a bar in the past!

00:06:01.060 --> 00:06:02.440
No, umm...

00:06:06.820 --> 00:06:09.490
You're too noisy! I was just getting to an important part!

00:06:09.490 --> 00:06:11.350
Who's the noisy one here?!

00:06:11.350 --> 00:06:13.070
Can't you see I'm busy singing?!

00:06:13.070 --> 00:06:14.850
Hey, both of you...

00:06:14.850 --> 00:06:17.550
It's an interview. Don't you think you should behave properly?

00:06:18.020 --> 00:06:19.370
Shut up!

00:06:19.370 --> 00:06:22.910
Anyway, what's your problem? What right do you have to interfere with my singing?!

00:06:22.910 --> 00:06:24.950
You don't have to put it that way...

00:06:23.700 --> 00:06:26.430
Let me talk about vegetables!

00:06:31.530 --> 00:06:36.260
Concerning that, I want you to pay attention to Squad 7's...

00:06:33.790 --> 00:06:36.260
<i>How long is she going to talk?</i>

00:06:38.220 --> 00:06:40.760
Please tell me about the Lieutenant.

00:06:40.760 --> 00:06:45.000
As a capable commander, he's the source of our bold battle plans.

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:47.380
He also has the initiative to carry them out.

00:06:47.770 --> 00:06:52.270
Not only that, he's impartial to all squad members, and he takes good care of us.

00:06:52.270 --> 00:06:56.560
He's also a broad-minded person with a moderate amount of humour. {lol, edit}

00:06:58.610 --> 00:07:01.350
I'm sorry, I said too much.

00:07:01.350 --> 00:07:03.310
That's the kind of person my brother is.

00:07:03.310 --> 00:07:04.670
<i>What, she's his family?</i>

00:07:04.670 --> 00:07:08.960
Don't forget that she's a civilian, so make sure that...

00:07:10.370 --> 00:07:11.510
About your squad leader...

00:07:11.870 --> 00:07:17.090
Let me see... If you're asking about my preference, he's rated above average.

00:07:17.090 --> 00:07:22.390
Hardness is the most important thing! And also, the elasticity and suppleness!

00:07:23.190 --> 00:07:27.210
Oh no, muscles! I'm talking about muscles!

00:07:27.680 --> 00:07:32.630
About who's the person with the muscles I like the most... It's a secret!

00:07:32.630 --> 00:07:35.470
Oh, my! I'm so embarrassed!

00:07:35.470 --> 00:07:39.320
<i>That's not what I was asking about in the first place...</i>

00:07:40.870 --> 00:07:43.100
So, about your squad leader...

00:07:43.100 --> 00:07:44.200
Oink.

00:07:49.520 --> 00:07:50.690
Umm...

00:07:50.690 --> 00:07:52.010
Oink!

00:07:54.510 --> 00:07:55.720
Umm...

00:07:57.650 --> 00:08:00.790
Please wait for a while! We'll be done soon.

00:08:00.790 --> 00:08:02.970
You're going to take pictures, right?

00:08:02.970 --> 00:08:09.670
Taking my picture from my right side at a 45 degree angle will give you the most beautiful shot!

00:08:09.670 --> 00:08:10.770
Aisha too! {check name}

00:08:10.770 --> 00:08:12.650
Wait, that's a radio...

00:08:12.650 --> 00:08:14.100
No way! Really?

00:08:14.100 --> 00:08:17.390
Then my picture won't show up in the newspaper?

00:08:17.390 --> 00:08:19.950
How do you take pictures with a radio?

00:08:19.950 --> 00:08:22.700
No way!

00:08:22.700 --> 00:08:25.290
<i>What's with this squad?</i>

00:08:28.530 --> 00:08:30.880
<i>Please, let me make it in time!</i>

00:08:34.380 --> 00:08:36.800
<i>I was too late!</i>

00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:41.950
Don't worry. I wasn't able to get any information that you'd be worried about.

00:08:41.950 --> 00:08:44.290
Oh, really? Thank goodne-

00:08:45.130 --> 00:08:47.090
She found out!

00:08:47.100 --> 00:08:50.450
<i>Now that it's come down to this, I have no other choice but to talk to him in person.</i>

00:08:50.450 --> 00:08:53.050
<i>To achieve my aim, I'll resort to any means!</i>

00:09:01.640 --> 00:09:04.950
<i>The time limit is until Miss Ellet gives up and leaves.</i>

00:09:05.780 --> 00:09:08.460
<i>Three days until the radio broadcast.</i>

00:09:09.220 --> 00:09:13.310
<i>Until then, I must do everything to hide Welkin's true nature.</i>

00:09:14.180 --> 00:09:17.980
<i>Before then, I have to get my scoop at all costs.</i>

00:09:22.210 --> 00:09:25.390
<i>I can't lose this battle!</i>

00:09:26.950 --> 00:09:30.340
Lieutenant Gunther, it seems you're hiding some secrets!

00:09:30.340 --> 00:09:32.420
Nothing like that!

00:09:33.610 --> 00:09:35.570
Can I sit beside you?

00:09:35.570 --> 00:09:36.880
No!

00:09:40.150 --> 00:09:42.160
What are you doing?

00:09:42.160 --> 00:09:44.030
Physical... examination?

00:09:50.090 --> 00:09:51.880
You found me?

00:09:51.880 --> 00:09:52.710
Teehee!

00:10:02.500 --> 00:10:05.120
Seriously, what's with her?

00:10:05.120 --> 00:10:09.710
Her vitality is amazing, isn't it? That's what you call the reporter's spirit.

00:10:09.710 --> 00:10:12.050
Why are you speaking like there's nothing to be concerned about?

00:10:12.050 --> 00:10:12.980
You're the party involved.

00:10:13.330 --> 00:10:20.010
But you know, since she tries so hard, I think it's okay if I help her a bit.

00:10:20.370 --> 00:10:24.540
Welkin, do you know how much trouble I went through?

00:10:24.540 --> 00:10:27.200
Well, you might be right...

00:10:27.200 --> 00:10:30.110
It's all for the sake of the Militia's reputation.

00:10:30.110 --> 00:10:32.290
Even though I feel a little sorry for Miss Ellet,

00:10:32.290 --> 00:10:36.800
I <i>definitely</i> won't leave your side until she gives up and leaves.

00:10:36.800 --> 00:10:38.170
That's my plan.

00:10:38.170 --> 00:10:41.990
Definitely, huh? But that might be a bit difficult...

00:10:42.360 --> 00:10:43.660
Why?

00:10:45.540 --> 00:10:47.770
Do you want to follow me inside?

00:10:48.850 --> 00:10:51.660
Sorry, but I'll be back soon.

00:10:51.660 --> 00:10:53.460
Never mind, just hurry up and get it over with.

00:11:02.800 --> 00:11:04.050
Hello!

00:11:05.150 --> 00:11:07.020
Hello...

00:11:09.890 --> 00:11:14.480
Let me warn you first. If you don't listen to what I say, I'll scream.

00:11:14.480 --> 00:11:16.920
What will the people who come running here think?

00:11:16.920 --> 00:11:19.410
Shouldn't it be the opposite?

00:11:19.410 --> 00:11:22.790
The one giving the threats should be keeping quiet.

00:11:25.800 --> 00:11:28.330
Plus, I'll tear off my clothes.

00:11:28.330 --> 00:11:29.560
Great plan, isn't it?

00:11:29.560 --> 00:11:31.820
I see. A woman's weapon, eh?

00:11:31.820 --> 00:11:36.480
Don't take it to heart. I just want to talk to you when that woman's not around.

00:11:37.060 --> 00:11:38.560
I understand how you feel.

00:11:38.560 --> 00:11:40.760
Well then, let the interview begin!

00:11:45.820 --> 00:11:46.890
He's slow.

00:11:47.800 --> 00:11:49.640
He's taking forever!

00:11:51.680 --> 00:11:55.940
<i>B-But... A maiden can't peep into the men's toilet!</i>

00:11:56.220 --> 00:12:00.370
I keep going to the toilet lately. It's a bother.

00:12:01.760 --> 00:12:05.740
<i>You can't, Alicia. Even it's to protect the Militia's reputation...</i>

00:12:05.740 --> 00:12:07.870
<i>I need to get married too, if I do this...</i>

00:12:08.230 --> 00:12:10.470
So, what's your secret?

00:12:10.470 --> 00:12:14.050
Well, it's not like I was trying to hide it or anything.

00:12:14.050 --> 00:12:17.130
Then what was that girl trying to hide?

00:12:18.050 --> 00:12:20.460
It's hard to explain it in words.

00:12:23.090 --> 00:12:26.470
Hey, Welkin, please.

00:12:26.920 --> 00:12:27.970
Wait!

00:12:30.640 --> 00:12:34.100
I want to know more about you.

00:12:34.100 --> 00:12:36.520
I want to understand you.

00:12:36.520 --> 00:12:39.050
In return, I'll do anything for you.

00:12:39.050 --> 00:12:40.630
So, please...

00:12:40.630 --> 00:12:41.500
Pl-e-a-se.

00:12:41.500 --> 00:12:42.130
Pl-e-a-se.

00:12:42.130 --> 00:12:42.840
Pl-e-a-se.

00:12:42.840 --> 00:12:43.240
Pl-e-a-se.

00:12:43.900 --> 00:12:47.370
Hey, the two of you! What are you doing in there!

00:12:50.260 --> 00:12:51.700
Interview.

00:12:53.050 --> 00:12:54.410
Looks like it's true...

00:12:55.060 --> 00:12:57.800
I was just getting to the good part...

00:12:57.800 --> 00:13:02.420
Have some common sense! How
can you interview him in a toilet?

00:13:02.420 --> 00:13:04.310
You came in too, so the same goes for you.

00:13:04.310 --> 00:13:05.770
What do you mean?

00:13:05.770 --> 00:13:08.890
Well, that makes it a draw for you two.

00:13:08.890 --> 00:13:10.800
And what do you mean by that?

00:13:10.800 --> 00:13:11.810
No, nothing, really.

00:13:12.380 --> 00:13:13.910
More importantly, Miss Ellet.

00:13:13.910 --> 00:13:15.520
What you said just now...

00:13:15.520 --> 00:13:17.400
Did you say you'll do anything for me.

00:13:17.400 --> 00:13:20.270
Oh, that. I did say something like that...

00:13:20.660 --> 00:13:22.820
Can I request a favour then?

00:13:30.080 --> 00:13:32.290
What's going on here?

00:13:32.290 --> 00:13:36.500
Right. She said she'd do anything for me, so I asked her.

00:13:36.500 --> 00:13:40.190
I said I wanted everyone to have some good food once in a while.

00:13:40.190 --> 00:13:42.630
But why meat?

00:13:42.630 --> 00:13:45.670
<i>I thought it was some big favour,</i>

00:13:45.670 --> 00:13:49.320
<i>but if this is enough to make him talk, it's small price to pay.</i>

00:13:49.320 --> 00:13:50.970
Everyone, listen up.

00:13:51.870 --> 00:13:56.750
The war correspondent, Miss Ellet,
supplied this meat for Squad 7 today.

00:13:56.750 --> 00:13:59.700
Be grateful to Miss Ellet and enjoy yourselves!

00:13:59.700 --> 00:14:00.410
That's all!

00:14:02.010 --> 00:14:06.320
But can we finish eating all of this?

00:14:04.580 --> 00:14:05.720
Oink.

00:14:06.730 --> 00:14:09.200
We'll call Faldio and his squad then.

00:14:13.700 --> 00:14:15.650
I feel bad about this.

00:14:15.650 --> 00:14:16.840
It's all right.

00:14:16.840 --> 00:14:18.390
It'd be a waste to leave anything behind.

00:14:18.390 --> 00:14:22.050
Why don't you interview us too?

00:14:22.050 --> 00:14:25.170
We have lots of good-looking men in our squad.

00:14:25.170 --> 00:14:27.170
When the time comes, sure.

00:14:28.400 --> 00:14:31.640
Everyone sure is eating a lot.

00:14:37.770 --> 00:14:40.440
Where did Hans go?{ZOMG SHE SPOKE!!!!}

00:14:46.370 --> 00:14:48.810
Are you telling me that my vegetables are inedible?

00:14:48.810 --> 00:14:50.030
No, I don't mean that...

00:14:50.030 --> 00:14:53.280
You're a man, aren't you? It's not good to be picky about food.

00:14:53.280 --> 00:14:55.330
Arrogant bastards.

00:14:55.330 --> 00:14:59.260
The elites of the Militia belongs to us, Squad 1.

00:14:59.260 --> 00:15:01.420
The interview pisses me off too.

00:15:01.420 --> 00:15:04.160
Why doesn't Faldio get the interview first?

00:15:04.160 --> 00:15:05.250
Exactly.

00:15:06.360 --> 00:15:10.940
It's all thanks to our squad leader that we get to eat such good food.

00:15:10.940 --> 00:15:13.700
That's right. You won't get the same
treatment with the other squad leaders.

00:15:19.620 --> 00:15:21.710
Delicious!

00:15:22.440 --> 00:15:24.020
It's a fight!

00:15:25.660 --> 00:15:27.650
A brat like you shouldn't get so stuck-up!

00:15:29.090 --> 00:15:31.050
You're all idiots!

00:15:33.600 --> 00:15:36.430
I definitely won't lose in a brawl.

00:15:36.430 --> 00:15:38.540
Everyone, give it your all!

00:15:40.830 --> 00:15:43.890
Show them the spirit of Squad 1!

00:15:46.980 --> 00:15:50.420
Don't do it! Fighting is a barbaric act. Stop it!

00:15:51.860 --> 00:15:54.030
What the hell, you fools!

00:15:54.030 --> 00:15:57.560
Do you want me to teach you the joy of men?!

00:16:23.430 --> 00:16:25.350
Oink...

00:16:25.350 --> 00:16:27.060
Rascal!

00:16:27.660 --> 00:16:29.310
Take this!

00:16:31.320 --> 00:16:34.720
Oh no, this is too intense!

00:16:35.060 --> 00:16:36.780
Everyone, stop it!

00:16:37.170 --> 00:16:39.470
Hey, Welkin! Say something!

00:16:41.340 --> 00:16:44.160
The two of them went over there.

00:16:44.160 --> 00:16:45.290
That idiot...

00:16:45.290 --> 00:16:48.850
Faldio, you're a squad leader too!

00:16:48.850 --> 00:16:50.350
It's not so bad, is it?

00:16:50.350 --> 00:16:51.190
Of course it's bad!

00:16:52.090 --> 00:16:55.160
I'm sure Welkin will think it's a good thing.

00:17:05.370 --> 00:17:07.280
You don't mind what's happening back there?

00:17:07.280 --> 00:17:09.700
Why not? Let them do it once in a while.

00:17:09.700 --> 00:17:12.330
It's better to let loose?

00:17:12.330 --> 00:17:14.230
Yeah, something like that.

00:17:19.550 --> 00:17:22.080
You don't behave like a soldier.

00:17:23.210 --> 00:17:25.840
Should I say... you're hard to classify...

00:17:25.840 --> 00:17:29.930
A normal soldier is stiffer and more arrogant.

00:17:29.930 --> 00:17:32.420
It'd be boring if everyone was the same, right?

00:17:32.420 --> 00:17:35.240
Besides, I'm not cut out for this.

00:17:38.680 --> 00:17:40.210
I thought so.

00:17:40.210 --> 00:17:42.890
This is what that girl was trying to hide.

00:17:42.890 --> 00:17:46.610
And you had a hard time because of that.

00:17:48.920 --> 00:17:51.670
<i>I see. So that's how it is.</i>

00:17:51.670 --> 00:17:54.430
I think I have a rough idea now.

00:17:54.430 --> 00:17:55.230
Huh?

00:17:55.230 --> 00:17:56.630
About what kind of person you are.

00:17:57.050 --> 00:17:57.850
Really?

00:17:57.850 --> 00:18:01.180
Just a little bit, though.

00:18:01.760 --> 00:18:03.850
Well, shall we begin then?

00:18:03.850 --> 00:18:07.170
Stop acting dumb. I'm talking about the interview!

00:18:07.170 --> 00:18:09.040
But, you said you know me already...

00:18:09.040 --> 00:18:11.610
Those are two entirely different matters.

00:18:11.610 --> 00:18:13.190
Come on, let's begin!

00:18:13.830 --> 00:18:15.230
O-Okay.

00:18:21.180 --> 00:18:26.100
It's too late. The Militia's reputation is going to fall.

00:18:26.100 --> 00:18:28.560
What are you grumbling about?

00:18:28.560 --> 00:18:31.330
No use crying over spilt milk, right?

00:18:31.330 --> 00:18:36.050
Rosie, you wouldn't understand how much trouble I had to go through.

00:18:36.050 --> 00:18:37.690
Hey, don't worry about it!

00:18:37.690 --> 00:18:39.140
Cross that bridge when you come to it!

00:18:39.140 --> 00:18:41.920
I'm depressed because we'll never come to it.

00:18:41.920 --> 00:18:42.750
Now, now...

00:18:42.750 --> 00:18:46.470
Anyway, thanks for your hard work, Alicia.

00:18:50.330 --> 00:18:51.860
It's starting!

00:18:59.520 --> 00:19:02.660
Irene Ellet's "On the Gallian Front"!

00:19:03.140 --> 00:19:05.020
<i>I'm sure she'll talk rot about us.</i>

00:19:05.020 --> 00:19:07.470
Well then, let's get the ball rolling.

00:19:07.470 --> 00:19:11.540
This time, I infiltrated the Gallian Army's Amatriain Base.

00:19:11.540 --> 00:19:20.230
The squad that I interviewed, Squad 7, is led by Lieutenant Welkin Gunther, a man I've secretly been watching.

00:19:20.230 --> 00:19:27.720
From the interviews, I could feel that he's a flexible man who's not bound by common sense.

00:19:28.060 --> 00:19:33.720
Furthermore, unlike normal soldiers, he treats all his solders equally and without discrimination.

00:19:33.720 --> 00:19:37.640
Am I hearing it wrong? I think she's praising us...

00:19:37.640 --> 00:19:40.560
No, you're not hearing it wrong.

00:19:39.050 --> 00:19:47.160
They'll definitely continue to lord over the Imperials and achieve more victories.

00:19:40.560 --> 00:19:42.200
She's definitely praising us.

00:19:48.510 --> 00:19:54.520
Well, I've talked a lot with him, but to be honest, I don't understand Welkin.

00:19:55.740 --> 00:19:57.750
So, that's about all.

00:19:57.750 --> 00:20:01.820
Squad 7, I'll be sure to go interview you again!

00:20:01.820 --> 00:20:03.510
I'll be counting on you again, then!

00:20:05.910 --> 00:20:08.410
You don't need to come again!

00:20:11.010 --> 00:20:12.570
Yo, sorry to keep you waiting.

00:20:12.570 --> 00:20:14.970
I'm Largo. Largo Potter.

00:20:14.970 --> 00:20:16.730
I'm actually thirty-six years old.

00:20:16.730 --> 00:20:23.000
I fought in the First War as well. But if it's 
up to fate, I'll probably have to fight again.

00:20:23.000 --> 00:20:25.420
But I'm definitely not a warmonger.

00:20:25.420 --> 00:20:29.550
I'm a gentle man who likes to play 
in the soil and grow vegetables.

00:20:29.920 --> 00:20:33.340
Next time on Valkyria Chronicles, Chapter 7.

00:20:33.340 --> 00:20:34.970
The Darcsen's Disaster.

00:20:34.970 --> 00:20:36.930
Vegetables won't betray man,

00:20:35.380 --> 00:20:40.000
Chapter 7:

00:20:35.380 --> 00:20:40.000
Darcsen`s Disaster

00:20:36.930 --> 00:20:40.050
so man shouldn't betray vegetables.
